Description: create bootable USB drives from ISO and disk images
 Rufus is a utility that helps format and create bootable USB flash drives,
 from Windows and Linux ISO images, disk images (compressed or not, VHD and
 VHDX) or FreeDOS. It can customize the installation of Windows 11, download
 Windows ISOs, add a persistent partition to Linux live drives and check drives
 for bad blocks.
 .
 This is an unofficial port of Rufus to Linux, with a Qt 6 user interface that
 runs natively under Wayland, and a command line interface (rufus-cli). It is
 not affiliated with or supported by the upstream Rufus project.
